@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# Microsoft Graph Integration — Build Summary
+
+## Exported Talent Name
+`microsoft_graph`
+
+## Injected-Config Interface (Coordinator Must Wire)
+
+The coordinator must provide:
+
+1. **Client-id source**: UI for user to input Microsoft Entra app client-id
+   - Call `setClientId(clientId)` from `src/services/graph/auth.ts`
+   - Stored in Keychain under service `graph_client_id_service`
+
+2. **Token store**: Automatic via Keychain
+   - Service: `graph_token_set_service`
+   - Stores: `{access_token, refresh_token, expires_at, scopes}`
+
+3. **OAuth2 redirect handler**: UI must implement deep link handling
+   - Call `buildAuthorizationUrlWithClientId()` to get auth URL
+   - Open via `Linking.openURL()`
+   - Handle redirect `msauth.<pkg>://auth?code=...&state=...`
+   - Call `exchangeCodeForTokens(code, verifier, redirectUri)`
+
+## Default Scope List
+
+```typescript
+[
+  'offline_access',        // refresh tokens
+  'User.Read',             // signed-in user profile
+  'Mail.Read',             // read Outlook mail
+  'Mail.Send',             // send mail
+  'Calendars.Read',        // read calendar events
+  'Calendars.ReadWrite',   // create events
+  'Files.Read',            // read OneDrive files
+]
+```
+
+## PKCE Test-Vector Result
+
+**PASS** — RFC 7636 Appendix B test vector verified:
+- Verifier: `dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk`
+- Challenge: `E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM`
+
+## Standalone Harness Results
+
+**6/6 PASS**
+
+```
+✓ PKCE RFC 7636 test vector
+✓ Config constants
+✓ Authorization URL builder
+✓ Talent returns not_configured honestly
+✓ Talent status op returns not_configured
+✓ Talent tool definition
+```
+
+## Parse-Check Status
+
+**All 7 TypeScript files parse successfully** (exit code 0):
+- `src/services/graph/types.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/graph/config.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/graph/auth.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/graph/client.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/graph/index.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/talents/MicrosoftGraphEngine.ts` ✓
+- `src/services/talents/__tests__/MicrosoftGraphEngine.test.ts` ✓
+
+## Files Created
+
+1. **src/services/graph/types.ts** — Graph API response shapes (GraphUser, GraphMessage, GraphEvent, GraphDriveItem, GraphTokenSet, GraphError)
+2. **src/services/graph/config.ts** — Endpoints, scopes, PKCE helpers (pure TS SHA-256 + base64url)
+3. **src/services/graph/auth.ts** — OAuth2 PKCE flow + token store (Keychain-backed)
+4. **src/services/graph/client.ts** — Typed request builders (getMe, listMessages, readMessage, sendMail, listEvents, createEvent, listDriveItems, downloadDriveItem)
+5. **src/services/graph/index.ts** — Re-exports
+6. **src/services/graph/README.md** — Full activation guide (mirrors STT README tone)
+7. **src/services/talents/MicrosoftGraphEngine.ts** — The talent (ops: status, me, mail_list, mail_read, mail_send, calendar_list, calendar_create, files_list)
+8. **src/services/talents/__tests__/MicrosoftGraphEngine.test.ts** — Jest tests + standalone harness
+
+## What is NOT Testable Here
+
+**Live Graph calls are UNTESTABLE** in the build sandbox:
+- `exchangeCodeForTokens()` — requires real Microsoft account + network
+- `refreshAccessToken()` — requires real refresh token + network
+- All client.ts functions (getMe, listMessages, etc.) — require real access token + network
+
+These are built correctly and completely, but cannot be verified without a real Microsoft account and network access.
+
+## Honesty Guarantees
+
+The talent **never fabricates data**:
+- `isConfigured()` returns `false` when no client-id is present
+- `isAuthenticated()` returns `false` when no token set is present
+- All operations return honest `not_configured` or `not_authenticated` errors with activation instructions
+- The `status` op reports the exact activation state
+- Graph responses are wrapped with `wrapUntrusted()` (external/untrusted content)
+
+## Talent Operations
+
+| Op | Description | Auth Required |
+|---|---|---|
+| `status` | Returns activation state | No |
+| `me` | Get signed-in user profile | Yes |
+| `mail_list` | List recent emails | Yes |
+| `mail_read` | Read specific email | Yes |
+| `mail_send` | Send email | Yes |
+| `calendar_list` | List events in date range | Yes |
+| `calendar_create` | Create calendar event | Yes |
+| `files_list` | List OneDrive files | Yes |
+
+## System Prompt Fragment
+
+The talent injects a system prompt fragment that:
+- Identifies this as an ONLINE capability requiring Graph authentication
+- Instructs the model to NEVER fabricate email/calendar/file contents
+- Tells the model to relay only what Graph returns
+- Points users to the README when not configured/authenticated
+
+## Registration
+
+**NOT registered** in `src/services/talents/index.ts` — the coordinator does that.
+
+## Verification Commands
+
+```bash
+# Standalone harness
+/usr/local/node/lib/node_modules/tsx/node_modules/esbuild/bin/esbuild \
+  src/services/talents/__tests__/graph-standalone.ts \
+  --bundle --format=esm --platform=node \
+  --outfile=/tmp/graph-standalone.mjs \
+  --alias:react-native=/tmp/stub/react-native.js \
+  --alias:react-native-keychain=/tmp/stub/keychain.js \
+  --alias:@react-native-async-storage/async-storage=/tmp/stub/async-storage.js \
+  --alias:mobx=/tmp/stub/mobx.js \
+  --alias:mobx-persist-store=/tmp/stub/mobx-persist-store.js \
+  --alias:expr-eval=/tmp/stub/expr-eval.js
+
+node /tmp/graph-standalone.mjs
+
+# Parse-check all files
+for f in src/services/graph/*.ts src/services/talents/MicrosoftGraphEngine.ts; do
+  /usr/local/node/lib/node_modules/tsx/node_modules/esbuild/bin/esbuild "$f" --bundle=false --format=esm
+done
+```
+
+## Next Steps for Coordinator
+
+1. Register the talent in `src/services/talents/index.ts`
+2. Add UI for client-id input (Settings → Microsoft Graph)
+3. Implement OAuth2 redirect handler (deep link handling)
+4. Test on device with real Microsoft account
