+# Microsoft Graph Integration — Activation Guide
+
+## Status
+
+The Microsoft Graph integration **seam is built and typed**. The types, PKCE auth flow, and request builders are complete, but the layer ships **NOT CONFIGURED**: no client-id is present, so `isConfigured()` returns `false` and all Graph operations return honest `not_configured` errors. Nothing fabricates mail, calendar, or file data.
+
+This is deliberate. Microsoft Graph requires a registered Microsoft Entra app (free) and user authentication via OAuth2 PKCE. The user must complete the activation steps below before any Graph call can fire.
+
+## What already works (no activation needed)
+
+- **Types**: `GraphUser`, `GraphMessage`, `GraphEvent`, `GraphDriveItem`, `GraphTokenSet`, `GraphError` — all Graph API response shapes are typed.
+- **PKCE helpers**: `generateCodeVerifier()`, `codeChallengeFromVerifier()` — pure TypeScript SHA-256 + base64url, no crypto dependencies.
+- **Auth flow**: `buildAuthorizationUrl()`, `exchangeCodeForTokens()`, `refreshAccessToken()` — OAuth2 PKCE flow via `fetch`.
+- **Request builders**: `getMe()`, `listMessages()`, `readMessage()`, `sendMail()`, `listEvents()`, `createEvent()`, `listDriveItems()`, `downloadDriveItem()` — typed wrappers for the Graph API.
+- **Talent**: `MicrosoftGraphEngine` — exposes `microsoft_graph` tool with ops: `status`, `me`, `mail_list`, `mail_read`, `mail_send`, `calendar_list`, `calendar_create`, `files_list`.
+
+## Activation checklist (user must do this)
+
+1. **Register a Microsoft Entra app** (free):
+   - Go to https://portal.azure.com/#blade/Microsoft_AAD_RegisteredApps/ApplicationsListBlade
+   - Click "New registration"
+   - Name: "PocketPal AI" (or whatever you like)
+   - Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts"
+   - Redirect URI: leave blank for now (we'll add it in step 3)
+   - Click "Register"
+   - Copy the **Application (client) ID** — you'll need it in step 5
+
+2. **Add API permissions**:
+   - In your app registration, go to "API permissions"
+   - Click "Add a permission" → "Microsoft Graph" → "Delegated permissions"
+   - Add these permissions:
+     - `User.Read` (signed-in user profile)
+     - `Mail.Read` (read Outlook mail)
+     - `Mail.Send` (send mail)
+     - `Calendars.Read` (read calendar events)
+     - `Calendars.ReadWrite` (create events)
+     - `Files.Read` (read OneDrive files)
+   - Click "Add permissions"
+   - **Do NOT click "Grant admin consent"** — these are delegated permissions, so the user consents at sign-in time
+
+3. **Add a mobile/desktop redirect URI**:
+   - In your app registration, go to "Authentication"
+   - Under "Platform configurations", click "Add a platform"
+   - Choose "Mobile and desktop applications"
+   - Redirect URI: `msauth.com.pocketpalai://auth` (replace `com.pocketpalai` with your app's package name)
+   - Click "Configure"
+
+4. **Build and install the app** on your device (the redirect URI must match the installed app's package name).
+
+5. **Supply the client-id**:
+   - Open the app
+   - Go to Settings → Microsoft Graph (you'll need to add a UI for this — see step 6)
+   - Paste the Application (client) ID from step 1
+   - The app stores it in Keychain
+
+6. **Add a UI for client-id input** (you must build this):
+   - Create a settings screen with a text input for the client-id
+   - Call `setClientId(clientId)` from `src/services/graph/auth.ts` when the user saves
+   - Optionally call `clearClientId()` to remove it
+
+7. **Implement the OAuth2 redirect handler** (you must build this):
+   - When the user taps "Sign in with Microsoft", call `buildAuthorizationUrlWithClientId()` to get the auth URL
+   - Open the URL in a browser (use `Linking.openURL()` from React Native)
+   - The user signs in and is redirected to `msauth.com.pocketpalai://auth?code=...&state=...`
+   - Your app must handle this deep link (add an intent filter in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`)
+   - Extract the `code` and `state` from the redirect URL
+   - Call `exchangeCodeForTokens(code, verifier, redirectUri)` to get the token set
+   - The token set is stored in Keychain automatically
+
+8. **Test** on your device with a real Microsoft account (personal or work/school).
+
+## The hard caveat — be honest with yourself here
+
+Microsoft Graph is an **ONLINE** capability. It requires:
+- A registered Microsoft Entra app (free, but you must do it)
+- User authentication via OAuth2 PKCE (you must implement the redirect handler)
+- Network access (the Graph API is at https://graph.microsoft.com)
+
+The talent honestly reports its activation state via the `status` op:
+- `not_configured`: no client-id in Keychain
+- `not_authenticated`: no token set in Keychain
+- `authenticated`: valid token set present
+
+If the talent reports `not_configured` or `not_authenticated`, tell the user they need to complete the activation steps above. **Never fabricate mail, calendar, or file data.**
+
+## Scopes
+
+The default scopes are minimal and documented in `src/services/graph/config.ts`:
+- `offline_access`: refresh tokens (so we don't re-auth on every launch)
+- `User.Read`: signed-in user profile (name, mail)
+- `Mail.Read`: read Outlook mail
+- `Mail.Send`: send mail
+- `Calendars.Read`: read calendar events
+- `Calendars.ReadWrite`: create events
+- `Files.Read`: read OneDrive files
+
+## PKCE test vector
+
+The PKCE helpers are unit-tested with the RFC 7636 Appendix B test vector:
+- Verifier: `dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk`
+- Challenge: `E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM`
+
+Run the standalone harness to verify:
+```bash
+/usr/local/node/lib/node_modules/tsx/node_modules/esbuild/bin/esbuild src/services/talents/__tests__/MicrosoftGraphEngine.test.ts --bundle --format=esm --platform=node --outfile=/tmp/graph.mjs --alias:react-native=/tmp/stub/react-native.js --alias:react-native-keychain=/tmp/stub/keychain.js --alias:@react-native-async-storage/async-storage=/tmp/stub/async-storage.js --alias:mobx=/tmp/stub/mobx.js --alias:mobx-persist-store=/tmp/stub/mobx-persist-store.js --alias:expr-eval=/tmp/stub/expr-eval.js
+node /tmp/graph.mjs
+```
+
+## What is NOT testable here
+
+The live Graph calls are **UNTESTABLE** in the build sandbox:
+- `exchangeCodeForTokens()` requires a real Microsoft account + network
+- `refreshAccessToken()` requires a real refresh token + network
+- `getMe()`, `listMessages()`, `readMessage()`, `sendMail()`, `listEvents()`, `createEvent()`, `listDriveItems()`, `downloadDriveItem()` — all require a real access token + network
+
+The PKCE helpers, config constants, URL builders, error-code mapping, and the talent's `not_configured`/`not_authenticated` error paths ARE testable offline. The standalone harness verifies those.
+
+## File ownership
+
+You may ONLY create/modify these files:
+- `src/services/graph/types.ts`
+- `src/services/graph/config.ts`
+- `src/services/graph/auth.ts`
+- `src/services/graph/client.ts`
+- `src/services/graph/index.ts`
+- `src/services/graph/README.md` (this file)
+- `src/services/talents/MicrosoftGraphEngine.ts`
+- `src/services/talents/__tests__/MicrosoftGraphEngine.test.ts`
+
+DO NOT register the talent in `src/services/talents/index.ts` — the coordinator does that.
