+    '- Each agency publishes a rating, outlook (positive / stable / negative), and periodic rationale reports.',
+    '- Ratings reflect a composite assessment of: institutional strength, economic structure, fiscal flexibility, monetary flexibility, external flexibility, and debt sustainability.',
+    '',
+    '### Key credit strengths',
+    '- **Diversified economy**: Larger and more diversified than many regional peers (not purely resource-dependent).',
+    '- **Strategic assets**: Suez Canal revenues, tourism receipts, and diaspora remittances provide structural FX inflows.',
+    '- **Natural gas**: Egypt has become a regional gas hub (Zohr field and other discoveries), with LNG export capacity and potential to supply Europe.',
+    '- **IMF program support**: An active IMF arrangement (typically an Extended Fund Facility, EFF) provides policy anchor and catalyses other official financing.',
+    '- **Large domestic market**: ~100 million+ population provides a consumption base and labour force.',
+    '',
+    '### Key credit vulnerabilities',
+    '- **High public debt**: Debt/GDP ratio is elevated, with significant domestic debt and rising debt-service costs.',
+    '- **Fiscal deficit**: Persistent primary deficits or narrow surpluses limit fiscal space.',
+    '- **FX vulnerability**: Reserve cover has been pressured by import needs, capital outflows, and debt-service obligations. Episodes of parallel-market premium have occurred.',
